{"questions":[{"question_id":"QFXd1WjgFpkZ1CpI","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"hydrogen","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"hydrogen-peroxide","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"hydrogen-peroxide-in-its-reaction-with-kio4-and-nh2oh-respec-2014-marks-1-qfxd1wjgfpkz1cpi.htm","content":"Hydrogen peroxide in its reaction with KIO<sub>4</sub> and NH<sub>2</sub>OH respectively, is acting as a","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"reducing agent, oxidising agent"},{"identifier":"B","content":"reducing agent, reducing agent"},{"identifier":"C","content":"oxidising agent, oxidising agent"},{"identifier":"D","content":"oxidising agent, reducing agent"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>In the reaction with potassium periodate (KIO<sub>4</sub>) and hydroxylamine (NH<sub>2</sub>OH), hydrogen peroxide (H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>) exhibits different roles :</p>\n\n<p>(i) When hydrogen peroxide reacts with potassium periodate (KIO<sub>4</sub>), it forms potassium iodate (KIO<sub>3</sub>).</p>\n\n<p><b>The balanced chemical reaction is :</b></p>\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -6.974ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"49.003ex\" height=\"8.569ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 21659.5 3787.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1186.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4F\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(811,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2623.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"munder\" transform=\"translate(3623.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(732.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4B\"></use><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-49\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"4F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4F\" transform=\"translate(1139,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1950,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtable\" transform=\"translate(0,-1200.9) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtr\" transform=\"translate(0,500)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">Potassium</text></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtr\" transform=\"translate(0,-550)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">periodate</text></g></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(7719.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"27F6\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-27F6\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"munder\" transform=\"translate(9635.5,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2023.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4B\"></use><use data-c=\"49\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N