/g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(811,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p>Oxidation state of oxygen in hydrogen peroxide :</p>\n\n<p>(a) In H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> :</p>\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -3.507ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.471ex\" height=\"8.145ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -2050 4628 3600\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtable\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtr\" transform=\"translate(0,1300)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"><g data-mml-node=\"mstyle\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1294.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2294.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3072.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(4128,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtr\" transform=\"translate(0,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtr\" transform=\"translate(0,-1300)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"><g data-mml-node=\"mstyle\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(849.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1905.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2683.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p>(b) In O<sub>2</sub> :</p>\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.442ex\" height=\"1.557ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 2405.6 688\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(849.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1905.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p>The oxidation state of oxygen increases from -1 to 0, indicating that H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub> is oxidized and acts as a reducing agent for KIO<sub>4</sub>.</p>\n\n<p>(iii) When hydrogen peroxide reacts with hydroxylamine (NH<sub>2</sub>OH), it produces nitric acid (HNO<sub>3</sub>) and water (H<sub>2</sub>O).</p>\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"36.614ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 16183.2 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-m